# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
# Recovery-only Gatekeeper bring-up for the AERA ramdisk.
#
# ROOT CAUSE THIS FIXES
# ---------------------
# The stock-derived rc declared the service `disabled`, so the ONLY thing that
# could ever start it was the property trigger:
#
#     on property:vendor.gatekeeper.is_security_level_spu=0
#
# That property is produced by device.mk via PRODUCT_VENDOR_PROPERTIES, which
# lands in /vendor/build.prop. This device builds a dedicated recovery ramdisk
# with PRODUCT_BUILD_VENDOR_IMAGE := false, and recovery's init loads only the
# ramdisk /prop.default for ro.* properties at property_init time; it does not
# mount /vendor during boot. So the property is absent, the trigger never fires,
# `gatekeeper-1-0` stays disabled, and TWRP's decrypt path gets "fail to get
# Gatekeeper service" AFTER it has already read the DE/SP metadata. That exact
# symptom is recorded in config/gatekeeper-inputs.json.
#
# WHAT CHANGED VS THE TARGET RC, AND WHY
# --------------------------------------
#  1. class hal added (keeping early_hal)
#       Recovery init runs `class_start hal`. Class early_hal is a normal-boot
#       concept and is never started in recovery, which is why the service had
#       no path up at all. Joining `hal` gives it a start that depends on
#       nothing but the class system.
#
#  2. `disabled` removed
#       A disabled service starts only from an explicit trigger. Decryption
#       must not hinge on a property arriving from a partition recovery does
#       not mount. scripts/ensure-gatekeeper-props.py now also puts the two
#       properties into the ramdisk /prop.default as defence in depth, but the
#       service must be able to come up on its own.
#
#  3. user/group left EXACTLY as the target specifies: system / system
#       config/gatekeeper-inputs.json records user=system, group=[system], and
#       that is what is kept here. Recovery's vendor/etc/ueventd.rc applies the
#       target DAC:
#           /dev/qseecom   0660 system drmrpc
#           /dev/qce       0660 system drmrpc
#           /dev/smcinvoke 0660 system drmrpc
#       The OWNER of every one of those nodes is `system`, so a process running
#       with uid=system matches the owner class and gets rw. The drmrpc group is
#       not required for gatekeeper, and adding it would deviate from the target
#       service identity for no benefit.
#
# The HIDL interface name/instance is unchanged, so
# android.hardware.gatekeeper@1.0::IGatekeeper/default registers as before and
# the VINTF fragment astonc.gatekeeper.xml stays valid.

service gatekeeper-1-0 /vendor/bin/hw/android.hardware.gatekeeper@1.0-service-qti
    class hal
    class early_hal
    user system
    group system
    seclabel u:r:recovery:s0

# Retained from the target rc. Now a redundant second chance rather than the
# single point of failure. `start` on an already-running service is a no-op.
on property:vendor.gatekeeper.is_security_level_spu=0
    start gatekeeper-1-0
